# AGENTS.md

## Project

Payments API. Go, PostgreSQL, sqlc, Kubernetes. One service, one team.

## Commands

```bash
make test          # unit + integration
make test-unit     # fast, no database
make lint          # golangci-lint
make generate      # sqlc generate
```

Run `make test-unit` before every commit. Run `make test` before opening a pull request.

## Layout

```text
cmd/api/                 composition root
internal/payments/       handler, service, domain
internal/db/sqlc/        generated queries, do not edit
internal/infrastructure/ adapters
```

New behavior goes in the feature package. Handlers do not query the database. Services own transactions.

## Rules

- Never edit files in `internal/db/sqlc/`. Change the `.sql` file and run `make generate`.
- Every query on tenant data must include the tenant identifier.
- Money is stored in minor units as `int64`. Never use `float64`.
- New endpoint? Add a negative test for the wrong tenant and the wrong role.
- Do not add a dependency without an ADR.

## Done

- `make test` passes.
- `make lint` passes.
- The pull request states the commands run and their output.
- Migrations have a rollback step.
